<section class="testimonial-area py-0">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <div class="testimonial-wrapper-two">
            <div class="row no-gutters" style=" visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight;row-gap: 30px;">
                <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 col-md-6 d-flex">
                    <img src="/webassets/images/elements/step-37.jpeg" alt="img">
                </div>
                <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 col-md-6 d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center pl-md-4">
                    <div class="testimonial-content-box bg_cover wow fadeInRight justify-content-center align-items-start  d-flex flex-column"
                         style="background-image: none !important; visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight;">
                        <p><span style="color: #000000;"><strong>Dry Food</strong></span></p>
                        <p>
                            <span style="color: #000000;">
                                When it comes to feeding our feline friends, the choice
                                between dry and wet food can be a puzzling one. Dry food, often seen as a convenient
                                and economical option, has its fair share of supporters and detractors.
                                Understanding the benefits and drawbacks of dry food can help cat owners make
                                informed decisions about their pet's nutrition.
                            </span>
                        </p>
                        <p style="font-weight: bold;">
                            <span style="color: #000000;">
                                Pros of Dry Food for
                                Cats:
                            </span>
                        </p>

                        <ol>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #000000;">
                                    <strong>Convenience</strong>: One of the most
                                    significant advantages of dry cat food is its convenience. It can be left out
                                    for cats to graze on throughout the day without the risk of spoilage, making it
                                    a favored choice for pet owners with busy schedules.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #000000;">
                                    <strong>Cost-Effectiveness:</strong>&nbsp;Generally,
                                    dry food is more economical than wet food. It comes in larger packages that last
                                    longer, offering more meals per dollar spent.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #000000;">
                                    <strong>Dental Health:</strong>&nbsp;Some
                                    veterinarians argue that the crunchy texture of dry food can help reduce tartar
                                    build-up on a cat's teeth, potentially contributing to better overall dental
                                    health.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #000000;">
                                    <strong>Less Messy:</strong>&nbsp;Dry food is less
                                    messy and easier to clean up than wet food, which can be a significant advantage
                                    in maintaining a clean feeding area.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                        </ol>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

</section>

<section class="testimonial-area pb-0    py-5"
         style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(77, 79, 95, 1), rgba(77, 79, 95, 1)) !important;">
    <div class="container py-3">
        <div class="testimonial-wrapper-two">
            <div class="row no-gutters" style="row-gap: 30px; visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight;">

                <div class="col-lg-6 order-1-class d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center pr-lg-4">
                    <div class="testimonial-content-box bg_cover wow fadeInRight justify-content-center align-items-start  d-flex flex-column"
                         style="background-image: none !important; visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight;">
                        <p style="font-weight: bold;">
                            <span style="color: #ffffff;">
                                Cons of Dry Food for
                                Cats:
                            </span>
                        </p>
                        <ol>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #ffffff;">
                                    <strong>Moisture Content:</strong>&nbsp;The most
                                    critical issue with dry food is its low moisture content. Cats naturally have a
                                    low thirst drive and derive much of their water intake from their food. A diet
                                    exclusively based on dry food can lead to dehydration and is often linked to
                                    urinary tract diseases.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #ffffff;">
                                    <strong>Carbohydrate Levels:</strong>&nbsp;Dry foods
                                    typically contain higher levels of carbohydrates than wet foods. High
                                    carbohydrate intake can lead to obesity and diabetes, conditions increasingly
                                    seen in domestic cats.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #ffffff;">
                                    <strong>Variability in Quality:</strong>&nbsp;The
                                    quality of dry food can vary significantly between brands. Some may use high
                                    levels of fillers and low-quality ingredients that offer less nutritional value
                                    to your cat.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <span style="color: #ffffff;">
                                    <strong>Palatability:</strong>&nbsp;While many cats
                                    enjoy dry food, some may find it less palatable than wet food. This can
                                    especially be a problem for picky eaters or cats with certain health issues that
                                    affect their appetite.
                                </span>
                            </li>
                        </ol>
                    </div>

                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 order-2-class  ">
                    <img src="/webassets/images/elements/step-43.jpeg" class="" alt="img">
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

</section>

